        <pubDate>Thu, 30 Jul 2026 18:53:29 GMT</pubDate>
        <guid isPermaLink="false">2082902415855202686</guid>
        <link>https://nitter.net/gdb/status/2082902415855202686#m</link>
      </item>
      <item>
        <title>we&apos;ve cut prices on luna by 80%, making it by far the most price-efficient model in its class. a lot of our research is about how to create incredibly efficient models for any given level of intelligence. excited to see what you all do with intelligence too cheap to meter!</title>
        <dc:creator>@gdb</dc:creator>
        <description><![CDATA[<p>we've cut prices on luna by 80%, making it by far the most price-efficient model in its class.<br>
<br>
a lot of our research is about how to create incredibly efficient models for any given level of intelligence.<br>
<br>
excited to see what you all do with intelligence too cheap to meter!</p>
<hr/>
<blockquote>
<b>OpenAI (@OpenAI)</b>
<p>
<p>We are committed to pushing the model frontier across cost efficiency, capability, and speed.<br>
<br>
Starting today, we are reducing prices for GPT-5.6 Luna by 80% and GPT-5.6 Terra by 20% , and offering a faster option for GPT-5.6 Sol in the API.<br>
<br>
Luna and Terra’s lower prices are reflected in how usage is counted in Codex and ChatGPT Work, so your usage goes further.</p>
<img src="https://nitter.net/pic/media%2FHOfepUra4AAUEZi.png" style="max-width:250px;" />


</p>
<footer>
— <cite><a href="https://nitter.net/OpenAI/status/2082878156483219672#m">https://nitter.net/OpenAI/status/2082878156483219672#m</a>
</footer>
</blockquote>]]></description>
        <pubDate>Thu, 30 Jul 2026 17:47:15 GMT</pubDate>
        <guid isPermaLink="false">2082885748337115632</guid>
        <link>https://nitter.net/gdb/status/2082885748337115632#m</link>
      </item>
      <item>
        <title>R to @gdb: we also are releasing fast mode for sol in the API (2.5x faster!) and decreased the price of terra by 20%. our north star is to provide the best price for any given level of intelligence, and to provide the maximum ceiling of intelligence.</title>
        <dc:creator>@gdb</dc:creator>
        <description><![CDATA[<p>we also are releasing fast mode for sol in the API (2.5x faster!) and decreased the price of terra by 20%.<br>
<br>
our north star is to provide the best price for any given level of intelligence, and to provide the maximum ceiling of intelligence.</p>]]></description>
        <pubDate>Thu, 30 Jul 2026 17:48:42 GMT</pubDate>
        <guid isPermaLink="false">2082886114235613634</guid>
        <link>https://nitter.net/gdb/status/2082886114235613634#m</link>
      </item>
      <item>
        <title>try asking codex to go beyond what you think possible</title>
        <dc:creator>@gdb</dc:creator>
        <description><![CDATA[<p>try asking codex to go beyond what you think possible</p>
<hr/>
<blockquote>
<b>Billy Howell (@billyjhowell)</b>
<p>
<p>Things are getting wackier in AI land. I usually give Codex a long "impossible" task before I go to bed, just to see how it does overnight. It finished my "impossible task" before I could shut down my computer....<br>
<br>
On a whim I asked it to build a custom dashboard to monitor my 3-D printer. I explained it would need to find the IP address of the printer on the local network.<br>
<br>
Literally 5 minutes later I was looking at this live dashboard with all this detailed information from my printer. <br>
<br>
The future is wild.</p>
<img src="https://nitter.net/pic/media%2FHOesvmNWUAAfjGh.jpg" style="max-width:250px;" />


</p>
<footer>
— <cite><a href="https://nitter.net/billyjhowell/status/2082824949195022403#m">https://nitter.net/billyjhowell/status/2082824949195022403#m</a>
</footer>
</blockquote>]]></description>
        <pubDate>Thu, 30 Jul 2026 16:21:15 GMT</pubDate>
        <guid isPermaLink="false">2082864105883586798</guid>
        <link>https://nitter.net/gdb/status/2082864105883586798#m</link>
      </item>

